    "result_text": "The full suite is green (the only test class is `AcceptanceTest`; the other two files are the `AcceptanceBase` and `AuditLogCapture` support classes).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `bulkSignupWarning` on the owner response with minimal structural impact:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema with `default: false`. The generated `OwnerDto` initializes to `false`, so the GET path (`RespondWithOwner`) returns `false` with no code change.\n\n2. **`.../owner/BulkSignup.java`** (new) \u2014 a small cohesive static helper (mirroring the existing `Namesakes` utility) that returns `true` when more than 80 *other* owners already share the new owner's registration date \u2014 the same accumulation path as the daily-limit rule.\n\n3. **`.../owner/RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 one added line calling the helper, keeping that method at CC 1.\n\nStructural impact was kept low: the only edited method gains a single non-branching line (`WMC_other = 0`, CC unchanged), and the new behaviour lives in its own tiny unit with no surrounding complexity. The `>80` branch isn't directly asserted by the acceptance test, but is implemented faithfully per the spec, and the `false` default branch is verified green.",
